      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we can pass some info here (like RequestAdapterOptions) indicating if we have that features required (or toggle enabled) then we can avoid double-initialization.\n\nDo we have access to what features is required at [`BackendGL::DiscoverPhysicalDevices`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/opengl/BackendGL.cpp;l\u003d56;drc\u003d04b384233ff1b695a826d1bc54b6ba4bec02aaca)\n\nIf so we can avoid the double-initialization using the feature approach.\n\nDifferent from ANGLETexgureSharing: I think it\u0027s that extensions availablity and toggles are cached at the the first `ContextEGL::Create`. They are inherited at the second `ContextEGL::Create` when actually creating the device. I don\u0027t really know details about ANGLETextureSharing, but I think that\u0027s the main issue",
